# PHASE 0 — Prove the value

**Time: one weekend. No database. No embeddings. No retrieval.**

Pick 3 statutes I actually have questions about. Get them as plain text by any means,
including manual copy-paste. Load full text into a long-context model. Streamlit chat box.

An Egyptian civil code is ~1,150 articles and fits in a long context window whole. If
this already answers my real questions well, a large part of the rest of this spec may
be unnecessary — say so rather than proceeding out of momentum.

**Deliverables**
- `scratch/phase0.py` — single file, under 150 lines
- 3 statutes as `.txt` in `data/raw/`
- A written list of 10 real questions I asked and how well it did

**Phase gate**
- I have asked it 10 genuine questions
- We have jointly decided whether full retrieval is warranted
- If yes: the failure modes observed here are written down and drive Phase 2 priorities

